    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46050" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζά</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, 
			Aeol.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διά</span>, rarely as Prep.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζὰ τὰν σὰν ἰδέαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					29.6
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(2).484.3
			</span></i> (Mytil.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζὰ νυκτός</span> ap.Jo.Gramm.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Comp.</u>
				3.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζὰ</span>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χῶρις ἔχην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sapph.
					<u>Oxy.</u>
					1787
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				3ii 18
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζαβάλλω, ζάημι</span>, etc.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> as Prefix (cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διά</span>), <i>very</i>, in 
				Ep.
			 Adjs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζαής, ζάθεος,
			ζάκοτος</span>, etc.; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζαμενέω,
				ζάπλουτος, ζάφελος</span>.</div>
